  "note": "The win came from R-Drop regularization (symmetric KL between two dropout passes on the local NxN sim matrix at α=0.5) stacked onto the DCL nll_cos loss — it lifted recall from 0.7384 (DCL-only, node 1) to 0.762 and was the only change that moved the metric. Everything else in the loss/scheduler space was flat or counter-indicated: swapping cosine for OneCycleLR (node 9 = 0.7618) and their mean-merge (node 12 = 0.7614) were within ~0.001, while relevance-graded positive weighting (0.744), multi-positive averaging (0.716), and soft-FN/category/multitask variants all regressed. The broader lesson: the DCL + vector-mined-negative pipeline itself caps this run (a sibling's plain in-batch MNR hit",
